WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Cloud Bigtable
is Google Cloud's NoSQL

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.650
database that's
optimized for use cases

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.240
with high numbers
of reads and writes

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.550
per second at low latency.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.270
In previous episodes, we learned
about Bigtable speed, scale,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.490
and reliability,
as well as how it's

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.250
being used for use cases like
personalization and fraud

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.570
detection.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.670
In this episode, we're
going to learn more about

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.860
how Bigtable can be used
in the ad tech industry.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.530
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:32.220
Have you ever browsed one
of your favorite websites

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.080
and seen an advertisement
that just happens

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.430
to align with your interests?

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.530
The advertising technology,
or ad tech industry,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.100
is all about the systems,
software, and tools

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.560
that advertisers use
to deliver digital ads

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.010
to potential customers.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.390
The goal of ad tech is to help
both publishers and advertisers

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.330
optimize their
online ad campaigns.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.970
Publishers, which could
include popular websites

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.910
and mobile apps, want to
monetize their digital space

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.590
by serving ads to their users.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.470
Advertisers on the
other hand, want

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.660
to optimize the
ROI of ad campaigns

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.820
for their products by
efficiently reaching

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.020
target customers.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.960
One of the most
popular ad tech models

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.170
is the open exchange, where
automated real-time bidding

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.170
options are used to decide which
ad appears in front of a user

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.220
as they load a page.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.300
Another important part of ad
tech is using the power of data

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.020
to help digital advertisers
reach the right audiences.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.000
Some examples of data
that might be helpful

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.920
include demographics, referring
sites, search queries,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.310
behavior on the site, and
interaction with ad content.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.690
When you go on a
publisher app or website,

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.390
the publisher might
send information

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.250
to an ad exchange
that will look you up

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.240
by identification or by
cohort and characteristics.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.770
Different ad tech
companies might

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.710
offer different solutions,
but the pattern of looking up

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.420
the user is similar.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.930
Sounds like a good case
for a key value store, no?

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.690
Bigtable is a great database
solution for ad tech companies

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.110
because of several key business
critical challenges they face.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.540
First, ad tech companies
need to make sure

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.550
that they can serve
ads as fast as possible

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.890
when a user opens a page.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.800
Delivering ads faster translates
to a better user experience,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.850
making potential customers
more likely to click on ads

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.000
and improve ROI for advertisers.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.760
In practice, this means
that many ad tech companies

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.560
need database requests
to have latency

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.620
on the order of single
digit milliseconds.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.000
Bigtable is a great
option for this use case

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.480
since it's designed to
support large numbers of reads

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.550
and writes per second
at low latency.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.630
Ad tech companies also need
a database that can scale.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.630
They might have billions of ad
requests per day and millions

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.650
of requests per second.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.290
This kind of extremely
high throughput

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.710
might overwhelm many on-premise
or traditional databases.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:50.160
Luckily, Bigtable is designed
for this exact use case.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.870
It supports up to
millions of read

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.060
and write requests per
second and can store up

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.740
to petabytes of data.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.480
Throughput can be
adjusted dynamically

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.000
by adding or removing
Bigtable nodes,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.742
each of which
provides up to 10,000

00:03:01.742 --> 00:03:04.200
additional queries per second
as well as additional storage

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.130
capacity.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.670
Ad tech companies also want to
focus on their core technology

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.320
like the machine
learning algorithms

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.080
used to optimize ad
placement, rather than worry

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.970
about how to manage
their underlying database

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.500
infrastructure.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.690
As a fully managed
database service,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.670
Bigtable makes it easy
for development teams

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:24.840
to focus on innovation rather
than reinventing the wheel.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.570
Bigtable replicates data
across multiple Google data

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:30.720
centers all around the world
to maintain high availability

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.360
and low latency for
users everywhere.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.220
This makes it easy
for ad tech companies

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.967
to seamlessly expand
to new markets

00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:38.550
without having to
worry about managing

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.370
the data centers themselves.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.300
Bigtable also handles backups.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.270
So ad tech companies
can easily recover

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.670
from application-level
data corruption, as well as

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:48.820
human error.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.090
Ad tech companies also
find Bigtable useful

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.640
because of how easy it is to
integrate with other Google

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.410
Cloud products.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.050
Some companies have used
Memorystore from Memcached

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.730
to cache frequently
queried data.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.720
This can help get latency down
to lower than one millisecond,

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.170
and also help optimize
Bigtable costs.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.240
Other companies have
also extensively used

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.480
BigQuery, Google Cloud's
large scale data warehouse

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.880
for storage and analysis.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:18.269
While Bigtable can handle very
high throughput at low latency,

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:21.480
BigQuery can be better for
large scale data analysis.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.460
In the ad tech
space, BigQuery can

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.990
be helpful for
data scientists who

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.080
may want to compile analytics
and dashboards to help

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.230
advertisers and publishers
meet their goals.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.000
Powerful and
complex queries that

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.850
may take several minutes to
complete with other databases

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.970
may take just seconds
with BigQuery.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.640
And finally, ad tech
companies rely heavily

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.980
on machine learning to take
the data that's available

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.930
and use it to better
connect advertisers

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.030
and potential customers.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.670
Vertex AI is Google
Cloud's unified machine

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.840
learning platform.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.230
It makes it easy for businesses
to build, deploy, and scale

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.440
ML models on Google's
infrastructure.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.620
As you can see, Bigtable's
speed, scalability,

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.650
and reliability make it a great
fit for the unique challenges

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.910
of ad tech.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.777
If you're curious to learn more,
take a look at the links below.

00:05:09.777 --> 00:05:11.610
Thanks for joining us
today, and take a look

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.080
at the other episodes
in the series

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.380
to learn more about Bigtable.

